From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u, winex11: a remote-support helper sees and types into the person's screen

A remote-support service's helper in a person's session (9624, 9625) does on
Windows what the person sees: BitBlt from the screen DC and DXGI Desktop
Duplication read the screen -- the lock and sign-in screens included -- and
SendInput types into it, so a technician can unlock the machine through the
on-screen lock screen, whose password goes to PAM as at the console (ADR
0010 pattern A). Here that screen is the person's compositor, whose
privileged socket sg-elevated-run --system names (SG_COMPOSITOR_PRIV):

- The helper is on the desktop of the display it was given (SG_WINSTATION in
  its Unix environment, WinSta0\sg-elevated-N), whatever desktop its starter
  named or had: a service starts it with its own, the display-less service
  station, where it drew and read nothing (the null driver; TightVNC's viewer
  saw black). Its input desktop is that desktop too (OpenInputDesktop, and so
  UOI_IO): VNC servers switch their threads to the input desktop before they
  read the screen, and the person's own desktop's windows are on an X server
  the helper has no part in.
- The screen capture (7857) connects to SG_COMPOSITOR_PRIV instead of
  WAYLAND_DISPLAY: the compositor's capture of what is on the screen. The
  compositor offers its real capture only to root and the Windows services'
  control group (sg-compositor -R), anyone else there the public one (lock
  screen black).
- SendInput (and SetCursorPos) go to the compositor's virtual keyboard and
  pointer, if it offers them -- the same grant -- and from there where the
  person's own keyboard and mouse would: the focused window, the lock screen
  while locked. Keys go by scan code (from the virtual key, the layout's
  table for the rest; KEYEVENTF_UNICODE as the key that makes the character),
  absolute moves over the compositor's layout. A new user driver entry,
  pSendInput; every other program's input goes to the wineserver as before.
- The socket must be served by the account its seat directory is named for
  (.../<uid>/priv.sock, SO_PEERCRED), so a socket put in its place gets
  nothing -- not a keystroke a technician types. (SG_SESSION_UID cannot say:
  1706 removes it from the environment once the process has joined.)

The compositor shows the person a frame round the screen while a helper
captures (sg-compositor -R).

Gate: sg-session's test/remote-support-gate.sh in a QA VM (TightVNC as a
service: the viewer sees the lock screen and unlocks it; the person's own
program and SYSTEM outside the services capture black and type into
nothing); test/tokensession-gate.sh for the helper's start. Mutant
SG_MUTANT_INJECT_SERVER_ONLY (the viewer's password reaches nothing).
