+/*
+ * A remote-support helper's input, to the screen the person sees (Stained Glass OS)
+ *
+ * A Windows service's per-session helper -- a VNC server's desktop half,
+ * AnyDesk's backend -- is started by the service in a person's session with
+ * SYSTEM's own token (CreateProcessAsUser after SetTokenInformation
+ * (TokenSessionId), wine-sg 9624/9625). On Windows it sees that session's
+ * screen, the lock and sign-in screens included, and types into it with
+ * SendInput, so a technician can unlock the machine. Here that screen is the
+ * session's compositor (sg-compositor), and sg-elevated-run --system tells the
+ * helper its privileged socket (SG_COMPOSITOR_PRIV). This file connects there
+ * (for sg_wlcapture.c too) and sends SendInput's keys and pointer to the
+ * compositor's virtual keyboard and pointer, which go where the person's own
+ * keyboard and mouse would: the focused window, the lock screen while locked.
+ *
+ * The compositor decides who may: root, and the SYSTEM account's processes in
+ * the Windows services' control group (its -R). It offers anyone else on its
+ * privileged socket -- the lock screen, an elevated program -- no virtual
+ * keyboard or pointer, and refuses every other account the socket itself.
+ * Without the offer, input goes to the wineserver as ever (the program's own
+ * windows), and nothing reaches the screen.
